{
  "_id": "proverbs7",
  "book": {
    "_id": "proverbs",
    "title": "Proverbs",
    "titleShort": "Prov.",
    "titleOfficial": "",
    "subtitle": "",
    "summary": "",
    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 7,
    "summary": "An immoral woman leads a man to destruction as an ox to the slaughter—The house of an adulterous woman is the way to hell.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "My son, keep my words, and lay up my commandments with thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Keep my commandments, and live; and my law as the apple of thine eye.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "1 Ne. 17:15 (3, 15); D&C 14:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Deut. 32:10 (7–10)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Bind them upon thy fingers, write them upon the table of thine heart.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "Deut. 6:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "Jer. 31:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Say unto wisdom, Thou art my sister; and call understanding thy kinswoman:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Alma 37:35."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 25
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "That they may keep thee from the strange woman, from the stranger which flattereth with her words.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "2 Ne. 28:22 (20–23)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For at the window of my house I looked through my casement,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And beheld among the simple ones, I discerned among the youths, a young man void of understanding,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Passing through the street near her corner; and he went the way to her house,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the twilight, in the evening, in the black and dark night:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Job 24:15."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Alma 10:25; 14:6; Moses 6:27; 7:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And, behold, there met him a woman with the attire of an harlot, and subtil of heart.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Lust; Sexual Immorality."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "(She is loud and stubborn; her feet abide not in her house:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Stubbornness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now is she without, now in the streets, and lieth in wait at every corner.)",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "D&C 10:27 (26–27)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So she caught him, and kissed him, and with an impudent face said unto him,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have peace offerings with me; this day have I payed my vows.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1,
            "text": "IE She cynically suggests her piety."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 1,
            "end": 6
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore came I forth to meet thee, diligently to seek thy face, and I have found thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have decked my bed with coverings of tapestry, with carved works, with fine linen of Egypt.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "The Hebrew probably indicates a fragrant wood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Come, let us take our fill of love until the morning: let us solace ourselves with loves.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the goodman is not at home, he is gone a long journey:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath taken a bag of money with him, and will come home at the day appointed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "With her much fair speech she caused him to yield, with the flattering of her lips she forced him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He goeth after her straightway, as an ox goeth to the slaughter, or as a fool to the correction of the stocks;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "OR suddenly; all at once."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Fornication."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Till a dart strike through his liver; as a bird hasteth to the snare, and knoweth not that it is for his life.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "Eccl. 9:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 96
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Hearken unto me now therefore, O ye children, and attend to the words of my mouth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let not thine heart decline to her ways, go not astray in her paths.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Alma 5:41."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For she hath cast down many wounded: yea, many strong men have been slain by her.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Her house is the way to hell, going down to the chambers of death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Whore."
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Prov. 5:4; Jacob 2:35 (27–35). TG Damnation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "proverbs8",
  "prevChapterId": "proverbs6",
  "volume": {
    "_id": "oldtestament",
    "title": "Old Testament",
    "titleShort": "OT",
    "titleOfficial": "The Old Testament"
  }
}